# Spec-driven development

- Product or process changes need a folder under `docs/work/YYYY-MM-DD-short-name/` with `spec.md`. Chat is not the contract.
- Parent agent orchestrates. Delegate to `spec-writer`, `planner`, `implementer`, `reviewer`, `codebase-explorer` as defined in `AGENTS.md`.
- `spec.md` = what, why, acceptance, out of scope. No stack or folder decisions unless they *are* the requirement.
- `plan.md` / `tasks.md` = how. Implementer follows tasks; does not rewrite the spec to fit the code.
- Do not call work complete without `reviewer` (or an equivalent human review) and notes in `evidence.md`.
- Parallel implementers only when they share no files.

Example: “add login” → spec-writer first. “typo in README” → still a 5-line spec in a work folder, then edit.
